\n- Iterates over all traces (line 1147-1261)\n- Classifies traces into two cases:\n  - **Case A (round > n_lift):** Traces with num_y=1 (num_x=1 in final rounds)\n  - **Case B (round <= n_lift):** Traces with num_y>1 that need interpolation\n- Builds column pointer arrays and collects metadata for batched interpolation\n- **No GPU calls in this phase**\n\n### **Phase 2 (Lines 1263-1301): Batched Interpolation**\n- **Single GPU kernel launch per MLE round:** `batched_interpolate_columns_gpu()`\n  - Takes all Case B traces and batches their column interpolation\n  - Input: descriptor arrays (`InterpColDesc`), all column pointers\n  - Output: single large interpolated buffer for all Case B traces\n- Creates temporary `big_buf: DeviceBuffer<EF>` that lives until end of Phase 3\n\n### **Phase 3 (Lines 1303-1497): Constraint & Interaction Evaluation**\n\n**For Case A (Late evaluation, num_y=1):**\n- **Logup (lines 1369-1389):** Monomial batch `LogupMonomialBatch::evaluate(1)`\n  - **2 kernel launches:** numerator + denominator monomial kernels\n  - **1 additional kernel launch:** reduction kernel\n  - Total: 3 kernel launches\n- **Zerocheck (lines 1390-1407):** Monomial batch `ZerocheckMonomialBatch::evaluate(1)`\n  - **1 kernel launch:** monomial evaluation\n  - **1 additional kernel launch:** reduction kernel\n  - Total: 2 kernel launches\n\n**For Case B (Early evaluation, num_y>1):**\n\n**(1) Logup constraints (lines 1411-1424):**\n- `evaluate_logup_batched()` partitions by `monomial_num_y_threshold`:\n  - **Low traces (num_y <= threshold):** `LogupMonomialBatch`\n    - 2 kernel launches (numer + denom monomial) + 1 reduction = **3 kernels**\n  - **High traces (num_y > threshold):** `LogupMleBatchBuilder` (DAG-based)\n    - 1 main MLE kernel + 1 reduction kernel = **2 kernels**\n\n**(2) Zerocheck constraints (lines 1426-1494):**\n- Partitions high num_y traces by monomial-to-rules ratio:\n  - **High DAG ratio (line 1445):** `ZerocheckMleBatchBuilder`\n    - 1 main MLE