lock handles ONE coset** by `blockIdx.y`\n\n**Algorithm (Lines 359-460):**\n- **Line 361:** `bool const is_identity_coset = (coset_idx == 0);`\n- **Lines 375-381:** Coset-specific precomputation\n- **Lines 417-442:** Main loop:\n  - Call `acc_interactions<1, NEEDS_SHMEM, false>()` with `is_identity_coset` runtime flag\n- **Lines 444-459:** Single-coset reduction\n\n#### Helper Device Function: `acc_constraints` / `acc_interactions`\n\n**Lines 32-138 (zerocheck_round0.cu):**\n```cuda\ntemplate <uint32_t NUM_COSETS, bool NEEDS_SHMEM>\n__device__ __inline__ void acc_constraints(\n    FpExt *__restrict__ constraint_sums,     // output [NUM_COSETS]\n    const NttEvalContext<NUM_COSETS> &eval_ctx,\n    const Fp *is_first,                      // [NUM_COSETS]\n    const Fp *is_last,                       // [NUM_COSETS]\n    uint32_t x_int,\n    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_lambda_pows,\n    const Rule *__restrict__ d_rules,\n    size_t rules_len,\n    const size_t *__restrict__ d_used_nodes,\n    size_t used_nodes_len,\n    size_t lambda_len\n)\n```\n\n**Operations:**\n- **Lazy decoding** of Rule header (op, flags, x operand)\n- **Evaluates DAG expressions** using `ntt_eval_dag_entry<NUM_COSETS, NEEDS_SHMEM>()`\n- **Supports ops:** ADD, SUB, MUL, NEG, INV, VAR\n- **Buffers intermediate results** in `eval_ctx.inter_buffer[z_index * buffer_stride + c]`\n- **Accumulates constraint sums** weighted by `lambda_pows` for constraint nodes\n\n#### Launcher Functions\n\n**zerocheck_round0.cu Lines 524-591: `launch_zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints<>`**\n\n**Lines 546-548:** Determines launch params:\n```cuda\nauto [grid, block] = coset_round0_config::eval_constraints_launch_params(\n    buffer_size, skip_domain, num_x, NUM_COSETS, max_temp_bytes, BUFFER_THRESHOLD, MAX_THREADS\n);\n```\n\n**Lines 555-575:** Launches kernel with shared memory calculated from block size\n\n**Lines 581-588:** Final reduction kernel:\n```cuda\nsumcheck::final_reduce_block_sums<<<NUM_COSETS * skip_domain, reduce_block, reduce_shmem>>>(\n    tmp_sums_buffer, output, num_blocks\n);\n```\n\n**coset_parallel launcher (Lines 598-665): `launch_zerocheck_coset_parallel<>`**\n\n- Similar structure but uses `coset_parallel_round0_config::eval_constraints_launch_params()`\n- Grid has 2D organization: `(grid.x, num_cosets)`\n- Final reduction: `<<<num_cosets * skip_domain, ...>>>`\n\n**Top-level dispatcher (Lines 667-717: `_zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints`)**\n\n**Lines 699-715:** Threshold-based dispatch:\n```cuda\nif (use_coset_parallel_mode(num_x, skip_domain)) {\n    // Coset-parallel mode: grid.y = num_cosets\n    return DISPATCH_BOOL_PAIR(launch_zerocheck_coset_parallel, ...);\n} else {\n    // Lockstep mode: single thread handles all cosets via NUM_COSETS template\n    return dispatch_zerocheck(num_cosets, is_global, needs_shmem, ...);\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Coset-Parallel vs. Lockstep Mode\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu` Lines 23-27, 475-477\n\n**Decision Threshold (Lines 27, 476-477):**\n```cuda\nconstexpr uint32_t COSET_PARALLEL_THRESHOLD = 32768; // 2^15\ninline bool use_coset_parallel_mode(uint32_t num_x, uint32_t skip_domain) {\n    return (num_x * skip_domain) < COSET_PARALLEL_THRESHOLD;\n}\n```\n\n**Coset-Parallel Mode** (when `num_x * skip_domain < 2^15`):\n- **Grid organization:** 2D grid with `grid.y = num_cosets`\n- **Utilization:** Better GPU utilization for small workloads\n- **Each block:** Handles ONE coset independently\n- **Advantage:** Avoids redundant iNTT for identity coset; parallelizes across cosets\n- **Memory:** More blocks active simultaneously\n\n**Lockstep Mode** (when `num_x * skip_domain >= 2^15`):\n- **Grid organization:** 1D grid (grid.y = 1)\n- **Thread handling:** Each thread handles ALL cosets in sequence (via NUM_COSETS template)\n- **Advantage:** Shared iNTT coefficient across cosets; fewer SMs needed\n- **Register pressure:** Compiles `NUM_COSETS` variants (1-4 cosets) to manage registers\n\n### 5. Data Structures and Per-AIR Work Items\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` Lines 122-138\n\n**`Round0AirWorkItem<'a, HS>`** is the minimal set of read-only references:\n- **`single_pk`**: Per-AIR proving key (contains constraint DAG, max degree, etc.)\n- **`selectors_cube`**: 3 × `num_x` matrix (is_first, is_transition, is_last per x)\n- **`public_values`**: Per-AIR public inputs\n- **`eq_3bs`**: Per-interaction challenge evaluations (indices into interaction array)\n- **`cached_mains`**: Trace parts from prior committed segments\n- **`common_main`**: Shared main trace (common to all AIRs in current segment)\n- **`eq_xis`**: Precomputed eq(x_i) for all i (hashmap by domain size)\n- **`d_lambda_pows`**: Global lambda challenge powers (shared across AIRs)\n- **`beta_pows`**: Global beta challenge powers (shared across AIRs)\n- **`max_temp_bytes`**: Per-thread memory budget for temp buffers\n\n**Construction (Lines 909-925):**\n```rust\nRound0AirWorkItem {\n    trace_idx,                          // Index in trace list\n    single_pk: &self.pk.per_air[*air_idx],\n    n,                                  // From self.n_per_trace[trace_idx]\n    selectors_cube: sel,                // From selectors_base[trace_idx]\n    public_values: pv,                  // From self.public_values_per_trace[trace_idx]\n    eq_3bs: eq3b,                       // From self.eq_3b_per_trace[trace_idx]\n    cached_mains: &air_ctx.cached_mains,\n    common_main: &air_ctx.common_main,\n    eq_xis: &self.eq_xis,              // Shared FxHashMap\n    d_lambda_pows,                      // Shared device buffer\n    beta_pows: &self.beta_pows,         // Shared slice\n    l_skip,                             // Global l_skip\n    constraint_degree: self.constraint_degree, // Global max degree\n    xi: &self.xi,                       // Global challenge vector\n    max_temp_bytes: per_thread_temp_bytes,\n}\n```\n\n**Load Balancing:** Work items sorted by `common_main.height()` descending (line 929) to distribute larger AIRs first across thread chunks.\n\n### 6. Batching Constraints for Multiple AIRs\n\n**Current Architecture (per work item):**\nEach AIR is processed independently:\n- One call to `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` per AIR\n- One call to `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` per AIR\n- Each launches separate kernels with per-AIR DAG and buffers\n\n**Batching Opportunities:**\n\n1. **Descriptor Arrays:** Multiple AIRs could be batched by:\n   - Creating per-AIR descriptors containing:\n     - `d_rules` pointer\n     - `rules_len`\n     - `buffer_size`\n     - `num_x`, `skip_domain`, `height`, `num_cosets`\n     - Output buffer pointers\n   - Single kernel launch with descriptor array + per-AIR thread block assignment\n\n2. **Current Coset Parallelism:** Exploits only coset parallelism (grid.y), not AIR parallelism. A 2D+ kernel could parallelize both.\n\n3. **Memory Layout:** Currently per-AIR buffers are separate. Batched approach would interleave AIR indices in buffer layouts.\n\n4. **Constraints:**\n   - Different AIRs may have different `skip_domain`, `num_x`, `num_cosets`, constraint degree\n   - Threshold-based dispatch (`use_coset_parallel_mode()`) is per-AIR\n   - May need block-per-AIR approach or careful padding/alignment\n\nThis analysis shows the Round 0 evaluation uses sophisticated per-AIR parallelism across OS threads but lacks kernel-level batching across multiple AIRs. Descriptor array batching would require careful handling of heterogeneous AIR parameters and buffer layout coordination."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2fb024d-582e-4612-82c1-d7c12af7ab35","uuid":"b06e72ab-84f1-4f8b-b62b-d30ac9db3e0d","timestamp":"2026-04-13T10:11:10.120Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the Round 0 constraint evaluation code path in the cuda-backend crate of this Rust project. I need to understand:\n\n1. The entry point and main loop structur