{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01E9pHhQPDd9VnuVqbo3HVfk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the proving key structure. The constraint DAG is already cached:\n- `AirDataGpu.zerocheck_round0: ConstraintOnlyRules<true>` — contains `d_rules`, `d_used_nodes`, `buffer_size`\n- These are the same rules used in `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu`\n\nThe interaction evaluation (`evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`) builds a SEPARATE DAG from the symbolic interactions. This interaction DAG is NOT cached — it's the `interaction_rules` field, but looking more carefully:\n\n\n`AirDataGpu.interaction_rules: InteractionEvalRules` — this has `inner: EvalRules` with `d_rules`, `d_used_nodes`, `buffer_size`.\n\nBut wait, checking `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` in round0.rs (lines 132-275), it takes `pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey` and `symbolic: &SymbolicConstraints`, then builds the interaction DAG from `symbolic.interactions` on the fly. It doesn't actually use `pk.other_data.interaction_rules` at all.\n\nSo `interaction_rules` is for GKR input evaluation and logup MLE sumcheck rounds, while Round 0 builds its own separate DAG because it uses a different evaluation strategy — NTT-based with coset parallelism and weighted sums of interaction expressions, versus the MLE kernel's per-interaction numer/denom evaluation. The Round 0 interaction DAG would need its own cached version, but looking at the code, it's using `d_rules` and `d_numer_weights` for the synthetic interactions DAG.\n\nSince the rule structure is deterministic given the AIR's symbolic interactions, I could add a `Round0InteractionRules` to `AirDataGpu` that caches the encoded rules on device, buffer size, and a mapping from interaction indices to their corresponding rule indices. At prove time, I'd compute the dynamic weights using this cached mapping plus the challenge-dependent values. This is feasible but requires changes to keygen, so I'll factor it into the plan.\n\nNow I'm ready to document the approach and update the task list.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":946,"cache_read_input_tokens":114753,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":946},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2fb024d-582e-4612-82c1-d7c12af7ab35","uuid":"e382828d-f306-4943-af5a-3bf15a4be566"}
