{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SE8robdB74SsrfxkZqNaiw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TzJadoYDvnpnFfWvCZ7wP5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-13-1600-batch-round0-descriptor-arrays\n\nReplace per-AIR Round 0 kernel launches with batched descriptor-array kernels for both zerocheck constraint evaluation and logup interaction evaluation. Currently, each of the ~310 AIRs per segment at APC 300 gets 2+ individual kernel launches, buffer allocations, and H2D copies, resulting in ~1500 kernel launches per segment — nsys profiling shows 76% of Round 0 wall time (294ms) is overhead, not GPU compute. By caching the interaction DAG structure at keygen and batching all per-AIR contexts into a single H2D upload + single kernel launch (using the proven descriptor-array pattern from MLE batch kernels), we expect to reduce Round 0 from 294ms to ~100ms at APC 300, saving ~190ms from STARK excl trace.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1345,"cache_read_input_tokens":131897,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1345},"output_tokens":41,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2fb024d-582e-4612-82c1-d7c12af7ab35","uuid":"685c8b02-4feb-4784-9c4b-afff5313c843"}
