{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are a plan reviewer for a CUDA GPU optimization project. Review the implementation plan following the review guideline.\n\nRead these files in order:\n1. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/review_guideline.md` — the review standard to follow\n2. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/context.md` — project context\n3. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md` — the task being planned\n4. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-13-1600-batch-round0-descriptor-arrays/plan.md` — the plan to review\n\nThen verify the plan's claims against the actual codebase:\n- Read `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (lines 90-280 for the Round 0 orchestration, and lines 830-970 for the full loop)\n- Read `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs` (full file) to verify the per-AIR functions\n- Read `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs` to verify the proving key structure\n- Read `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu` (at least the coset-parallel kernel and the launcher function)\n- Read `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle.rs` lines 110-230 to see the existing batch pattern\n\nCheck the plan against the actual code for:\n1. Are the file paths and line numbers correct?\n2. Does the proposed batched kernel correctly handle the intermediate buffer layout?\n3. Is the interaction DAG caching approach sound? Does the plan correctly identify what's static vs dynamic?\n4. Is the memory budgeting approach realistic given the prealloc-round0-buffers failure (which showed ~1GB max buffer per thread)?\n5. Does the `THREADS_PER_BLOCK = 256` choice work for all AIR sizes? What about AIRs where skip_domain * x_per_block doesn't divide nicely into 256?\n6. Is the reduction kernel design correct — can the existing `batched_final_reduce_block_sums` be adapted?\n7. Are the performance estimates realistic?\n\nReturn your response in the format: Findings, Improvements, Assessment.\n\nBe concrete and precise. Reference file paths and line numbers. Do NOT accept vague claims."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012iXBoiGLntjUndbWKRicBY","session_id":"f2fb024d-582e-4612-82c1-d7c12af7ab35","uuid":"49bddf61-06a3-4105-902e-864a4e44a929","timestamp":"2026-04-13T10:23:16.551Z"}
