{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BcgpDpGQwQEerf1UEgL1oP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-13-1600-batch-round0-descriptor-arrays\n2\t\n3\tReplace per-AIR Round 0 kernel launches with batched descriptor-array kernels for both zerocheck constraint evaluation and logup interaction evaluation. Currently, each of the ~310 AIRs per segment at APC 300 gets 2+ individual kernel launches, buffer allocations, and H2D copies, resulting in ~1500 kernel launches per segment — nsys profiling shows 76% of Round 0 wall time (294ms) is overhead, not GPU compute. By caching the interaction DAG structure at keygen and batching all per-AIR contexts into a single H2D upload + single kernel launch (using the proven descriptor-array pattern from MLE batch kernels), we expect to reduce Round 0 from 294ms to ~100ms at APC 300, saving ~190ms from STARK excl trace.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012iXBoiGLntjUndbWKRicBY","session_id":"f2fb024d-582e-4612-82c1-d7c12af7ab35","uuid":"762162f2-5ae0-4fb9-b5a7-d1b71d2fae58","timestamp":"2026-04-13T10:23:20.908Z"}
