{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K6ZA9TRcgFZ2tEbbBjfte9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Batch Round 0 Descriptor Arrays\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tReplace per-AIR Round 0 kernel launches (zerocheck constraint eval + logup interaction eval) with batched descriptor-array kernel launches, eliminating ~1500 kernel launches per segment at APC 300. This directly targets the worst-scaling component: Round 0 takes 294ms at APC 300 vs 177ms at APC 0 (gets SLOWER with more APCs), with nsys profiling showing 76% of wall time is per-AIR overhead (buffer allocation, kernel launch, H2D/D2H copies, CPU DAG construction), not GPU compute.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### Entry Point\n10\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` line 899: Round 0 evaluation within `prove_zerocheck_and_logup_gpu`.\n11\t\n12\t### Main Loop (lines 899-966)\n13\t1. **Phase 1 (lines 899-926)**: Build `Vec<Round0AirWorkItem>` — one per trace. Pure CPU.\n14\t2. **Line 929**: Sort work items by descending height.\n15\t3. **Lines 939-943**: Choose `num_threads = 8` if ≥ 100 AIRs, else 1.\n16\t4. **Lines 944-966**: Multi-thread via `std::thread::scope`. Each thread processes its chunk of AIRs sequentially via `process_air_round0()`.\n17\t\n18\t### Per-AIR Processing: `process_air_round0()` (lines 140-272)\n19\tFor each AIR, sequentially:\n20\t1. `SymbolicConstraints::from()` — CPU: build constraint representation from proving key (line 144)\n21\t2. `main_parts.to_device()` — H2D: upload trace pointers (line 162)\n22\t3. `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` — GPU: 1 eval kernel + 1 reduction kernel + 3 buffer allocations (intermediates, temp_sums, sp_evals) (lines 168-181, defined in round0.rs lines 31-124)\n23\t4. `sum_buffer.to_host_on_current_stream()` — D2H (line 184)\n24\t5. CPU: transpose + iDFT + polynomial construction (lines 185-208)\n25\t6. `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` — CPU: build synthetic interaction DAG + compute weights. GPU: 1 eval kernel + 1 reduction kernel + 5 buffer allocations (rules, numer_weights, denom_weights, intermediates, temp_sums, s_evals) (lines 214-229, defined in round0.rs lines 132-275)\n26\t7. `sum.to_host_on_current_stream()` — D2H (line 232)\n27\t8. CPU: unzip, transpose, iDFT, polynomial construction (lines 233-261)\n28\t\n29\t### Bottleneck Analysis (APC 300, 310 AIRs/segment)\n30\tPer segment, the current code executes:\n31\t- ~620 kernel launches (310 AIRs × 2 evals, each with eval + reduction)\n32\t- ~2000+ DeviceBuffer allocations (via global MemoryManager mutex)\n33\t- ~620 H2D copies (main_parts, rules, weights per AIR)\n34\t- ~620 D2H copies (results per AIR)\n35\t- ~310 CPU DAG constructions for interaction eval (SymbolicDagBuilder + SymbolicRulesGpu::new)\n36\t\n37\tNsys data: Total Round 0 GPU kernel time = 564ms across all streams. With 8 threads, ideal wall time would be ~30ms. Actual = 294ms. Overhead = 264ms (76%).\n38\t\n39\t### CUDA Kernels\n40\t- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu`: `zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_coset_parallel_kernel` — 539 instances, 238ms total GPU time\n41\t- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu`: `logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_coset_parallel_kernel` — 396+339=735 instances, 249ms total GPU time\n42\t\n43\t### Existing Pattern to Follow\n44\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle.rs` lines 113-218: `ZerocheckMleBatchBuilder` — collects per-AIR `BlockCtx` + `ZerocheckCtx` on CPU, uploads once, launches one batched kernel for all AIRs. Uses `air_block_offsets` for the reduction phase.\n45\t\n46\t## Changes\n47\t\n48\t### Change 1: Cache interaction DAG structure at keygen\n49\t\n50\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs`\n51\t\n52\tAdd a new struct to `AirDataGpu`:\n53\t```rust\n54\tpub struct Round0InteractionRules {\n55\t    /// Encoded interaction DAG rules, pre-computed and uploaded at keygen.\n56\t    pub d_rules: DeviceBuffer<u128>,\n57\t    pub buffer_size: u32,\n58\t    /// For each interaction: the rule_idx of its `count` expression.\n59\t    pub count_rule_idxs: Vec<usize>,\n60\t    /// For each interaction: the rule_idxs of its message field expressions.\n61\t    /// message_rule_idxs[interaction_idx][field_idx] = rule_idx\n62\t    pub message_rule_idxs: Vec<Vec<usize>>,\n63\t    /// Number of rules (= length of weight vectors).\n64\t    pub rules_len: usize,\n65\t}\n66\t```\n67\t\n68\tAdd field `pub interaction_round0: Option<Round0InteractionRules>` to `AirDataGpu`.\n69\t\n70\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/pkey.rs` (in the keygen function that populates `AirDataGpu`)\n71\t\n72\tFor each AIR with interactions, run the same DAG construction currently in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu` (lines 154-212 of round0.rs):\n73\t1. Build `SymbolicDagBuilder` from `symbolic.interactions`\n74\t2. Create `SymbolicRulesGpu::new()`\n75\t3. Encode and upload rules\n76\t4. Extract the interaction-to-rule-idx mappings\n77\t5. Store as `Round0InteractionRules`\n78\t\n79\tThis moves ~310 DAG constructions per segment from prove-time to keygen-time (once per AIR, amortized).\n80\t\n81\t### Change 2: Add `Round0ZcCtx` and `Round0LogupCtx` CUDA descriptor structs\n82\t\n83\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu`\n84\t\n85\tAdd a `#[repr(C)]` / `extern \"C\"` descriptor struct:\n86\t```cuda\n87\tstruct Round0ZcCtx {\n88\t    EvalCoreCtx eval_ctx;   // {selectors, preprocessed, main_parts, public_values}\n89\t    FpExt *d_eq_cube;\n90\t    FpExt *d_lambda_pows;\n91\t    Rule *d_rules;\n92\t    size_t *d_used_nodes;\n93\t    size_t rules_len;\n94\t    size_t used_nodes_len;\n95\t    size_t lambda_len;\n96\t    uint32_t buffer_size;\n97\t    Fp *d_intermediates;     // offset into shared intermediates buffer\n98\t    uint32_t skip_domain;\n99\t    uint32_t num_x;\n100\t    uint32_t height;\n101\t    uint32_t num_cosets;\n102\t    Fp g_shift;\n103\t    FpExt *tmp_sums_offset;  // offset into shared tmp_sums buffer\n104\t    FpExt *output_offset;    // offset into shared output buffer\n105\t};\n106\t```\n107\t\n108\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu`\n109\t\n110\tAdd analogous `Round0LogupCtx` with additional fields for `numer_weights`, `denom_weights`, `denom_sum_init`, and `FracExt *` output/tmp pointers.\n111\t\n112\tBoth files: reuse the existing `BlockCtx` struct from `batch_mle.cu` (or define a compatible one).\n113\t\n114\t### Change 3: Write batched Round 0 zerocheck constraint eval kernel\n115\t\n116\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu`\n117\t\n118\tNew kernel: `batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`\n119\t- **Grid**: `(total_blocks, 1)` — 1D grid\n120\t- **Block**: `THREADS_PER_BLOCK = 256`\n121\t- **Per-block logic**:\n122\t  1. Load `BlockCtx` from `d_block_ctxs[blockIdx.x]` → get `air_idx`, `local_block_idx`\n123\t  2. Load `Round0ZcCtx` from `d_zc_ctxs[air_idx]`\n124\t  3. Compute `coset_idx = local_block_idx / num_x_blocks` and `x_block_idx = local_block_idx % num_x_blocks`\n125\t  4. Compute `x_per_block = THREADS_PER_BLOCK / skip_domain`\n126\t  5. Thread maps: `ntt_idx = threadIdx.x % skip_domain`, `x_offset = threadIdx.x / skip_domain`\n127\t  6. Execute same evaluation loop as existing coset-parallel kernel: iterate x_int from `x_block_idx * x_per_block + x_offset` to `num_x`, stepping by `x_per_block`. Early-exit if `x_int >= num_x`.\n128\t  7. Block-level reduction, write to `ctx.tmp_sums_offset[local_tmp_offset]`\n129\t\n130\tNew launcher: `_batched_zerocheck_r0_eval_constraints`\n131\t- Takes `d_block_ctxs`, `d_zc_ctxs`, `total_blocks`, `THREADS_PER_BLOCK`\n132\t- Launches batched kernel + batched reduction kernel\n133\t\n134\t**Reduction kernel**: Adapt the existing `sumcheck::batched_final_reduce_block_sums` (from batch_mle.cu) to handle per-AIR `num_cosets * skip_domain` output dimensions. Grid: `(num_airs, max_cosets * skip_domain)`.\n135\t\n136\t**Note on intermediates buffer**: In the batched kernel, each block reads from `ctx.d_intermediates`. The `d_intermediates` pointer per AIR already points to the correct offset in a shared pre-allocated buffer (see Change 5).\n137\t\n138\t**Handling `GLOBAL` vs `NEEDS_SHMEM`**: Use only the `GLOBAL=true` code path for the batched kernel. The shared-memory optimization (`NEEDS_SHMEM`) is most useful for very small buffer_sizes where the kernel is already fast. The per-AIR launch variant still exists for fallback (see Change 6).\n139\t\n140\t### Change 4: Write batched Round 0 logup interaction eval kernel\n141\t\n142\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu`\n143\t\n144\tNew kernel: `batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`\n145\t- Same 1D grid structure as Change 3\n146\t- Per-block: load `Round0LogupCtx`, compute coset/x indices, evaluate interaction expressions using the cached `d_rules` and per-AIR `numer_weights`/`denom_weights`\n147\t- Block-level reduction writes `FracExt` (numer + denom) to `ctx.tmp_sums_offset`\n148\t\n149\tNew launcher: `_batched_logup_r0_eval_interactions`\n150\t\n151\t### Change 5: Rust orchestration — batched Round 0\n152\t\n153\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n154\t\n155\tReplace the multi-threaded per-AIR loop (lines 935-966) with a batched approach. New helper function `evaluate_round0_batched()`:\n156\t\n157\t**Phase A: Build descriptors (single thread, CPU only)**\n158\tFor each work item:\n159\t1. Compute `num_x = 1 << n_lift`, `num_cosets_zc`, `num_cosets_logup`\n160\t2. Determine if AIR is \"small\" (uses coset-parallel mode: `num_x * skip_domain < 32768`) or \"large\" (lockstep). Large AIRs are processed individually via existing per-AIR functions (Change 6).\n161\t3. For small AIRs, compute per-AIR block count: `blocks_per_air = ceil(num_x / x_per_block) * num_cosets` where `x_per_block = THREADS_PER_BLOCK / skip_domain`\n162\t4. Build `BlockCtx` entries and `Round0ZcCtx` for constraint eval\n163\t5. Compute per-AIR intermediate buffer size, accumulate total\n164\t6. For interaction eval: load cached `d_rules` from `pk.other_data.interaction_round0`. Compute dynamic `numer_weights`, `denom_weights`, `denom_sum_init` from `eq_3bs` and `beta_pows` using cached rule-idx mappings. Store in flat arrays.\n165\t7. Build `Round0LogupCtx` for interaction eval\n166\t\n167\t**Phase B: Allocate and upload**\n168\t1. Allocate single `intermediates_zc: DeviceBuffer<F>` sized for all small AIRs' constraint eval intermediates\n169\t2. Allocate single `intermediates_logup: DeviceBuffer<F>` for all small AIRs' interaction eval intermediates\n170\t3. Allocate `tmp_sums_zc` and `tmp_sums_logup` buffers\n171\t4. Allocate output buffers: `output_zc: DeviceBuffer<EF>` and `output_logup: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>`\n172\t5. Backfill intermediate/tmp_sums/output pointers into context structs\n173\t6. Upload: `d_block_ctxs_zc`, `d_zc_ctxs`, `d_block_ctxs_logup`, `d_logup_ctxs`, `d_air_offsets_zc`, `d_air_offsets_logup`, all weights\n174\t\n175\t**Phase C: Launch kernels**\n176\t1. Launch `_batched_zerocheck_r0_eval_constraints`\n177\t2. Launch `_batched_logup_r0_eval_interactions`\n178\t3. D2H copy all constraint results\n179\t4. D2H copy all interaction results\n180\t\n181\t**Phase D: CPU post-processing (parallel via rayon)**\n182\tFor each small AIR:\n183\t1. Extract constraint result slice from batched output\n184\t2. Transpose + iDFT → zerocheck polynomial\n185\t3. Extract interaction result slice from batched output\n186\t4. Unzip Frac, transpose + iDFT → logup numer/denom polynomials\n187\t\n188\t**Memory budgeting**: If total intermediate buffer size exceeds a threshold (e.g., 4 GB), split small AIRs into sub-batches by memory. Process each sub-batch with Phases B-D. This prevents the OOM that killed the prealloc-round0-buffers task.\n189\t\n190\t### Change 6: Fallback for large AIRs\n191\t\n192\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n193\t\n194\tAIRs that use the lockstep kernel path (`num_x * skip_domain >= 32768`) continue to use the existing per-AIR `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu` and `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`. These are few in number (typically < 20 at APC 300, ~20 at APC 0) and already saturate the GPU individually.\n195\t\n196\tProcess large AIRs BEFORE the batched small AIRs, sequentially on the main thread. This ensures large AIRs get full GPU bandwidth.\n197\t\n198\t### Change 7: Rust FFI bindings\n199\t\n200\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n201\t\n202\tAdd `#[repr(C)]` Rust structs matching the CUDA descriptors:\n203\t```rust\n204\t#[repr(C)]\n205\tpub struct Round0ZcCtx { /* fields matching CUDA struct */ }\n206\t\n207\t#[repr(C)]\n208\tpub struct Round0LogupCtx { /* fields matching CUDA struct */ }\n209\t```\n210\t\n211\tAdd FFI extern declarations and safe wrapper functions for the batched launchers.\n212\t\n213\t## Invariants\n214\t\n215\t1. **Correctness**: The batched kernel must produce identical results to the per-AIR kernel for every AIR. The computation per block is identical to one block of the existing coset-parallel kernel.\n216\t2. **Memory safety**: All device pointers in context structs must be valid for the duration of the kernel launch. The shared intermediates buffer must be sized to hold all AIRs simultaneously within a sub-batch.\n217\t3. **No regression at APC 0**: Large AIRs (lockstep mode) use the existing per-AIR path. The batched path only handles small AIRs. At APC 0 with ~20 AIRs/segment, most are large → minimal batching → no regression.\n218\t4. **Numerical equivalence**: The batched kernel uses GLOBAL intermediates mode only (no shared memory optimization). This may produce slightly different floating-point results due to different intermediate buffer layouts. Verify via prove+verify correctness test.\n219\t5. **Keygen compatibility**: The new `Round0InteractionRules` field in `AirDataGpu` is computed at keygen. Existing serialized proving keys are not affected (this field is not serialized; it's computed in-memory).\n220\t\n221\t## Measurement Plan\n222\t\n223\t1. Run `run_pairing.sh` for APC {0, 100, 300} before and after the change.\n224\t2. Analyze with `spec.py` to compare STARK excl trace and Round 0 sub-metrics.\n225\t3. Run nsys profiling for APC 300 to verify kernel launch count reduction.\n226\t4. Verify prove+verify passes for all 3 APC configs.\n227\t\n228\tExpected results:\n229\t- Round 0 APC 300: 294ms → ~100ms (2-3x improvement)\n230\t- Round 0 APC 0: 177ms → ≤ 177ms (no regression; large AIRs use existing path)\n231\t- STARK excl trace APC 300: 1409ms → ~1215ms (190ms improvement)\n232\t\n233\t## Rollback Criteria\n234\t\n235\t1. Round 0 at APC 300 improves by less than 60ms (< 20% of current 294ms)\n236\t2. STARK excl trace at APC 0 regresses by more than 30ms\n237\t3. Prove+verify fails for any APC configuration\n238\t4. GPU OOM error during batched kernel launch\n239\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012iXBoiGLntjUndbWKRicBY","session_id":"f2fb024d-582e-4612-82c1-d7c12af7ab35","uuid":"dd98a257-f7f7-4472-96a9-b47a85ef9866","timestamp":"2026-04-13T10:23:21.353Z"}
