{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FjGKzUH9YgNLxwQCyY4NVP","type":"tool_result","content":"332\t// Uses acc_constraints<1, NEEDS_SHMEM> with explicit parameter passing.\n333\t// Use when num_x * skip_domain is small for better GPU utilization.\n334\ttemplate <bool GLOBAL, bool NEEDS_SHMEM>\n335\t__global__ void zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_coset_parallel_kernel(\n336\t    FpExt *__restrict__ tmp_sums_buffer,   // [num_blocks][num_cosets * skip_domain]\n337\t    const Fp *__restrict__ selectors_cube, // [3][num_x]\n338\t    const Fp *__restrict__ preprocessed,\n339\t    const Fp *const *__restrict__ main_parts,\n340\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ eq_cube, // [num_x]\n341\t    const FpExt *__restrict__ d_lambda_pows,\n342\t    const Fp *__restrict__ public_values,\n343\t    const Rule *__restrict__ d_rules,\n344\t    size_t rules_len,\n345\t    const size_t *__restrict__ d_used_nodes,\n346\t    size_t used_nodes_len,\n347\t    size_t lambda_len,\n348\t    uint32_t buffer_size,\n349\t    Fp *__restrict__ d_intermediates,\n350\t    uint32_t skip_domain,\n351\t    uint32_t num_x,\n352\t    uint32_t height,\n353\t    Fp g_shift\n354\t) {\n355\t    extern __shared__ char smem[];\n356\t    FpExt *shared_sum = reinterpret_cast<FpExt *>(smem);\n357\t    Fp *ntt_buffers_base =\n358\t        NEEDS_SHMEM ? reinterpret_cast<Fp *>(smem + blockDim.x * sizeof(FpExt)) : nullptr;\n359\t\n360\t    uint32_t const l_skip = __ffs(skip_domain) - 1;\n361\t    uint32_t const num_cosets = gridDim.y;\n362\t\n363\t    // Each x_int group within the block gets its own ntt_buffer slice\n364\t    uint32_t const x_int_in_block = threadIdx.x >> l_skip;\n365\t    Fp *ntt_buffer = NEEDS_SHMEM ? (ntt_buffers_base + x_int_in_block * skip_domain) : nullptr;\n366\t\n367\t    // Thread layout: ntt_idx varies fastest, then x_int\n368\t    uint32_t const tidx = threadIdx.x + blockIdx.x * blockDim.x;\n369\t    uint32_t const ntt_idx = tidx & (skip_domain - 1);\n370\t    uint32_t const x_int_base = tidx >> l_skip;\n371\t\n372\t    // KEY DIFFERENCE: coset_idx from blockIdx.y\n373\t    uint32_t const coset_idx = blockIdx.y;\n374\t\n375\t    // Precompute values for this single coset\n376\t    uint32_t const ntt_idx_rev = rev_len(ntt_idx, l_skip);"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DJZrRxfovuAPecnesbZeka","session_id":"f2fb024d-582e-4612-82c1-d7c12af7ab35","uuid":"a9b3bcd7-77f1-4c74-a9ab-4241c1099ff8","timestamp":"2026-04-13T13:07:52.292Z"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a8c7ae03301d4a676","tool_use_id":"toolu_01DJZrRxfovuAPecnesbZeka","status":"completed","output_file":"","summary":"Final review of updated plan","usage":{"total_tokens":40907,"tool_uses":19,"duration_ms":115656},"uuid":"04b7d09a-939c-495f-af8b-cf98dd07628d","session_id":"f2fb024d-582e-4612-82c1-d7c12af7ab35"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DJZrRxfovuAPecnesbZeka","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have everything I need. Let me write up the findings.\n\n---\n\n## Findings\n\n### New Issue 1 (Design-level): Logup g_coset formula is not specified in Change 5\n\nChange 5 writes: \"For coset_idx > 0: `g_coset = g_shift^(...)` and `skip_ntt = false`.\"\n\nThe `(...)` is a placeholder. The existing logup coset-parallel kernel (`logup_round0.cu` line 376) uses `pow(g_shift, coset_idx)` — not `pow(g_shift, coset_idx + 1)` as in the zerocheck kernel (line 388). The formulas differ because zerocheck maps coset 0 → `g^1`, coset 1 → `g^2`, etc. (no identity coset), while logup maps coset 0 → identity, coset 1 → `g^1`, coset 2 → `g^2`, etc. Change 4 is correct and explicit about zerocheck. Change 5 never writes the formula; an implementor reading only the plan and copying the zerocheck formula would introduce a correctness bug. This needs to be made explicit: `g_coset = (coset_idx == 0) ? Fp::one() : pow(g_shift, coset_idx)`.\n\nThis is a minor specification gap — the formula is implied by \"matching logup_round0.cu lines 361-436\" in Invariant 6 — but Invariant 6 is the invariants section, not the implementation section. The implementation section (Change 5) must be self-contained.\n\n**Severity**: low — implementable with the codebase reference, but an explicit omission in an otherwise detailed spec.\n\n---\n\n### Verification of the three carried-over blockers\n\n**Blocker 1 — FracExt reduction (reinterpret_cast + d = 2×num_cosets×skip_domain)**: RESOLVED.\n\n`logup_round0.cu` lines 578-581 and lines 650-653 both confirm:\n```cpp\nsumcheck::final_reduce_block_sums<<<2 * large_domain, reduce_block, reduce_shmem>>>(\n    reinterpret_cast<FpExt *>(tmp_sums_buffer), reinterpret_cast<FpExt *>(output), num_blocks\n);\n```\nwhere `large_domain = num_cosets * skip_domain`. The plan's specification in Change 5 and Invariant 7 matches exactly.\n\n**Blocker 2 — buffer_stride vs max_temp_bytes**: RESOLVED.\n\n`eval_config.cuh` lines 47-55 confirm the reduction mechanism:\n```cpp\nsize_t num_x_per_thread = std::max(\n    div_ceil(desired_intermed_capacity_bytes, std::max(max_temp_bytes, (size_t)1)), (size_t)1\n);\nif (num_x_per_thread <= grid.x) {\n    grid.x = grid.x / num_x_per_thread;\n}\n```\nWith `max_temp_bytes = SIZE_MAX`, `desired_intermed_capacity_bytes / SIZE_MAX` rounds down to 0, `std::max(..., 1) = 1`, and `grid.x` is not reduced. The plan's prescription to pass `usize::MAX` is correct and sufficient to prevent grid reduction.\n\n**Blocker 3 — Zerocheck coset formula**: RESOLVED.\n\n`zerocheck_round0.cu` line 388 confirms: `Fp const g_coset = pow(g_shift, coset_idx + 1);` — this is exactly what the plan specifies in Change 4 step 7.\n\n---\n\n## Improvements I Would Consider\n\nNone that affect prototype correctness. The one gap (Issue 1 above) is a spec precision problem, not a design flaw. The plan's architecture, memory model, kernel structure, and reduction pattern are all sound and consistent with the existing codebase patterns.\n\n---\n\n## Assessment\n\n**Prototype-ready: yes**, with one caveat.\n\nThe three design-level blockers from Reviews 1 and 2 are fully resolved. The FracExt reinterpret pattern is correctly specified and matches the codebase. The `usize::MAX` trick correctly prevents `eval_config.cuh` from shrinking the grid. The zerocheck coset formula matches line 388 exactly.\n\nThe single remaining gap is in Change 5: the logup `g_coset` formula for `coset_idx > 0` is written as `g_shift^(...)`. The actual formula from `logup_round0.cu` line 376 is `pow(g_shift, coset_idx)` — different from zerocheck's `coset_idx + 1` because logup's coset 0 is the identity coset. An implementor working only from the plan would have to look this up. The fix is one line: replace `g_shift^(...)` with `pow(g_shift, coset_idx)` in Change 5. This is not a blocker given the codebase reference in Invariant 6, but it is the last place in the plan where a concrete implementation detail is left to the reader's inference.\n\nThe strongest part of the plan is the `buffer_stride` treatment: storing it as a per-context field and calling `_zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size` with `usize::MAX` ensures both the allocation size and the kernel's indexing arithmetic are derived from the same unreduced `num_x_blocks`, which is the exact correctness invariant the batched kernel depends on."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a8c7ae03301d4a676 (use SendMessage with to: 'a8c7ae03301d4a676' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 41927\ntool_uses: 19\nduration_ms: 115657</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2fb024d-582e-4612-82c1-d7c12af7ab35","uuid":"5241b6d2-e228-4965-ad79-17a4226d81fc","timestamp":"2026-04-13T13:08:21.302Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are a CUDA GPU optimization plan reviewer. This is the THIRD and final review iteration.\n\nPrevious reviews found these blockers (now claimed to be fixed):\n- Review 1: Wrong eval context type, unspecified buffer_stride, reduction heterogeneity\n- Review 2: FracExt reduction unspecified, buffer_stride vs max_temp_bytes mismatch, wrong zerocheck coset formula\n\nRead the updated plan:\n`/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-13-1600-batch-round0-descriptor-arrays/plan.md`\n\nAlso read the review guideline for the output format:\n`/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/review_guideline.md`\n\nThen verify all 5 previous blockers are resolved by checking against the codebase:\n\n1. **FracExt reduction** (Review 2 blocker 1): The plan now specifies reinterpret_cast + d=2*num_cosets*skip_domain. Verify this matches the existing pattern in `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu` — search for \"reinterpret_cast\" near the final_reduce calls.\n\n2. **buffer_stride vs max_temp_bytes** (Review 2 blocker 2): The plan now passes usize::MAX