{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ur8zcEfJFCipGKHL9SqyvB","type":"tool_result","content":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-13-1600-batch-round0-descriptor-arrays\n\nReplace per-AIR Round 0 kernel launches with batched descriptor-array kernels for both zerocheck constraint evaluation and logup interaction evaluation. Currently, each of the ~310 AIRs per segment at APC 300 gets 2+ individual kernel launches, buffer allocations, and H2D copies, resulting in ~1500 kernel launches per segment — nsys profiling shows 76% of Round 0 wall time (294ms) is overhead, not GPU compute. By caching the interaction DAG structure at keygen and batching all per-AIR contexts into a single H2D upload + single kernel launch (using the proven descriptor-array pattern from MLE batch kernels), we expect to reduce Round 0 from 294ms to ~100ms at APC 300, saving ~190ms from STARK excl trace.\n\n=== plan.md ===\n# Plan: Batch Round 0 Descriptor Arrays\n\n## Goal\n\n=== baseline ===\napc000.json\napc100.json\napc300.json\nnsys_apc000.nsys-rep\nnsys_apc000.sqlite\n\n=== current measurements ===\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc000.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc100.json\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_apc300.json\n\n=== nsys profile ===\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_nsys_apc300.nsys-rep\n/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/current_nsys_apc300.sqlite\n\n=== no source code modified ===\n .../plan.md                                        |  16 +-\n autoopt-results/logs/20260413-120204-13-1-plan.log | 204 +++++++++++++++++++++\n 2 files changed, 213 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2fb024d-582e-4612-82c1-d7c12af7ab35","uuid":"32347d43-a72e-4b18-96ca-17ac8e4c7322","timestamp":"2026-04-13T13:08:44.327Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== task.md ===\n# 2026-04-13-1600-batch-round0-descriptor-arrays\n\nReplace per-AIR